  "id": "sport",
  "term": "sport",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, sport is an embodied activity in which athletes act and make judgments through ongoing contact with the environment, other people, and sometimes technology, not only through visual, physiological, or cognitive processes. It can therefore be studied as a setting where touch, movement-related bodily sensing, and socially organized interaction shape perception, regulation, and skilled action.",
